WEBVTT

00:07.782 --> 00:13.542
Let's laugh and cry.
chanto waraimasho, nakimasho

00:14.142 --> 00:19.732
Subs originally by Froth-Bite
Manually retyped by #Retrofit@IRC.Rizon.Net
Raws by Darkside-Raws
We need to fill up our hearts.
kokoro no nakami wo juujitsu sasenakuccha

00:19.772 --> 00:28.322
Making matching memories with you...
anata to osoroi no omoide tsukuruno ga

00:28.322 --> 00:30.192
...is important.
daiji daiji

00:31.472 --> 00:34.022
Sometimes I become...
sunao ni narenakattari

00:34.352 --> 00:37.852
...almost dishonest and mean
ijiwaru shichaisouna hi aruno

00:39.352 --> 00:40.692
That's because...
sore wa...

00:42.692 --> 00:45.442
I love you and adore you,
daisuki de taisetsu de

00:45.572 --> 00:48.782
and I don't want to be apart from you.
hanaretaku nai sei nano nante

00:50.742 --> 00:51.742
That's the truth.
henne

00:54.292 --> 01:01.002
I just want to cuddle...
hontou wa itsumo nuku nuku shitetai

01:01.332 --> 01:03.342
...with you.
futaride

01:04.342 --> 01:10.052
So let's laugh and cry.
dakara waraimashou, nakimashou

01:10.722 --> 01:16.142
We need to keep our hearts warm.
kokoro no ondo wo atatame awanakucha

01:16.352 --> 01:24.782
The fate that made us meet...
anata to deaeta unmei ho subetega

01:24.782 --> 01:26.482
...is important.
daiji daiji

01:52.822 --> 01:54.782
<i>What can you do!?</i>

01:56.412 --> 02:00.702
<i>I want to do whatever makes Kozue-chan happy.</i>

02:03.912 --> 02:08.212
Oh yeah, I dozed off.

02:08.922 --> 02:11.922
Princess Oneboshi

02:14.592 --> 02:17.092
I can't show this to anyone yet.

02:17.852 --> 02:20.102
You can't show what to anyone?

02:23.932 --> 02:25.602
What do you have behind your back, Shiratori?

02:25.982 --> 02:27.022
Nothing!

02:29.772 --> 02:33.322
Is this the story you're writing?

02:33.902 --> 02:35.362
Yes, it is.

02:35.362 --> 02:37.662
That's great.

02:37.662 --> 02:38.702
It's not really...

02:38.702 --> 02:40.832
So, what kind of story is it?

02:41.662 --> 02:43.162
Don't give me that!

02:43.162 --> 02:45.832
Children's stories always have pictures and a plot!

02:46.872 --> 02:48.792
I'll listen to it.

02:48.792 --> 02:50.042
Don't be stingy!

02:50.042 --> 02:54.092
If you are a writer of children's literature, you need to show your work to others!

02:55.222 --> 02:57.592
Well, I'm not really done yet...

02:57.592 --> 02:59.552
I don't care.

03:00.142 --> 03:01.302
Just do it.

03:01.932 --> 03:03.102
Fine.

03:04.852 --> 03:09.232
One day, a prince who was bored, left his castle and went out for a picnic.

03:09.632 --> 03:14.302
During his picnic, he received a sketchbook from sharky Tamami-gon,

03:14.322 --> 03:16.862
and a set of crayons from Duke Frog.

03:17.612 --> 03:19.362
I'm sure they will come in handy.

03:19.372 --> 03:20.952
Thank you, Duke Frog.

03:20.952 --> 03:21.952
No problem.

03:21.952 --> 03:24.662
Now, your highness, have a good picnic.

03:25.042 --> 03:31.542
This is the story of how the prince did not go on an adventure, chase bandits, or slay a dragon,

03:31.542 --> 03:33.672
but instead just went on an ordinary picnic.

03:44.852 --> 03:47.182
The prince went on a picnic, huh?

03:47.182 --> 03:48.352
So, what happens next?

03:50.152 --> 03:51.442
Uh, well.

03:51.442 --> 03:53.482
He meets a princess.

03:53.482 --> 03:58.362
But Princess Umeboshi, who lived by herself in a castle, had a big secret.

03:58.362 --> 03:59.242
A secret?

03:59.662 --> 04:04.282
One day, the princess ate her favorite food, umeboshi...

04:04.282 --> 04:07.702
Mmmmm, it's so sour!

04:07.702 --> 04:09.162
That looks tasty.

04:09.162 --> 04:10.002
Oh?

04:10.712 --> 04:12.582
Here, have one.

04:12.592 --> 04:13.962
Thank you.

04:13.962 --> 04:16.962
"Munch. Shudder!" went the princess in the mirror.

04:16.962 --> 04:18.762
It's so sour!
"Munch. Shudder!" went the princess in the mirror.

04:18.762 --> 04:19.502
It's so sour!

04:22.012 --> 04:22.512
Oh?

04:23.642 --> 04:24.512
Oh?

04:25.142 --> 04:27.352
Now, there were two real princesses!

04:28.732 --> 04:32.352
That's how there are now two princesses.

04:33.312 --> 04:34.772
And right about now, they're both still saying...

04:34.772 --> 04:36.772
"It's so sour!"

04:37.112 --> 04:39.192
I see, so that's how it goes.

04:39.192 --> 04:41.532
So, then what happens, Shiratori?

04:41.862 --> 04:43.952
Yeah, let me continue.

04:43.952 --> 04:44.872
Let's see...

04:45.702 --> 04:50.202
Now, the two princesses lived happily in the castle.

04:50.662 --> 04:55.132
Today, they are having umeboshi time on a bridge over a small pond.

04:55.132 --> 04:57.922
"Munch. Mmmm, sour!"

04:57.922 --> 05:04.222
Right then, an umeboshi rolls off one of the princesses' hand, and into the pond.

05:05.222 --> 05:08.142
"Munch. Mmmmm!"

05:19.742 --> 05:20.442
Oh?

05:20.532 --> 05:21.242
Oh?

05:21.322 --> 05:22.362
Oh?

05:22.362 --> 05:24.702
Now there are three princesses.

05:25.912 --> 05:27.992
Yay! Princess!

05:28.372 --> 05:29.452
Yay! Yay!

05:29.452 --> 05:30.042
Princess!

05:30.122 --> 05:30.582
Princess!

05:30.662 --> 05:32.002
Princess!

05:32.002 --> 05:32.622
So? So?

05:32.622 --> 05:33.832
What's next?

05:33.832 --> 05:35.292
I want to hear more! More! More!

05:35.292 --> 05:36.612
Okay,
I want to hear more! More! More!

05:36.612 --> 05:36.632
Please! Please read more!
Okay,
I want to hear more! More! More!

05:36.632 --> 05:36.752
Please! Please read more!

05:36.752 --> 05:38.272
but I can't read it if you don't sit down.
Please! Please read more!

05:38.272 --> 05:38.302
but I can't read it if you don't sit down.

05:38.302 --> 05:39.672
More!
but I can't read it if you don't sit down.

05:39.672 --> 05:41.422
Oh, right.

05:43.882 --> 05:45.302
I sat down.

05:45.302 --> 05:47.972
You sit down too.

05:47.972 --> 05:48.642
Yeah.

05:49.972 --> 05:52.062
Now, hurry, hurry!

05:53.482 --> 05:57.312
And here is the story of the three Princesses Umeboshi!

05:57.312 --> 05:58.272
Yay!

05:58.402 --> 05:59.192
Yay!

05:59.272 --> 05:59.982
Yay!

06:00.482 --> 06:01.862
Aww.

06:01.862 --> 06:06.362
I want to hear Shiratori Onii-chan's story too.

06:10.702 --> 06:12.162
Mom...

06:12.162 --> 06:12.912
You're right.

06:13.412 --> 06:14.462
Asami.

06:14.462 --> 06:16.422
Then, the princess' shadow goes...

06:16.712 --> 06:17.712
Looks yummy...

06:17.712 --> 06:20.342
I want to eat it too.

06:20.342 --> 06:22.342
Here you go, it's good.

06:22.342 --> 06:24.802
But I don't have a mouth.

06:27.052 --> 06:28.342
That's it!

06:29.102 --> 06:31.312
It tickles!

06:31.312 --> 06:32.602
Done!

06:32.892 --> 06:37.442
The three princesses drew a face and dress for the shadow.

06:37.442 --> 06:38.732
Thank you!

06:38.732 --> 06:40.612
Now I can eat umeboshi.

06:45.952 --> 06:47.532
Delicious!

06:51.742 --> 06:55.292
And so now, there are four princesses in the castle.

06:56.372 --> 06:58.082
It's so sour!

06:59.632 --> 07:00.252
Correct!

07:00.632 --> 07:02.382
Perfect job, Princess!

07:02.382 --> 07:05.012
She must not be anything but a princess!

07:05.342 --> 07:07.342
She has both pretty and proper attire.

07:07.342 --> 07:08.512
She's perfect!

07:09.182 --> 07:11.012
Really?

07:13.772 --> 07:16.142
A man!

07:21.062 --> 07:21.942
Chiyuri-chan.

07:26.072 --> 07:27.442
That's correct.

07:27.452 --> 07:28.572
Good.

07:29.072 --> 07:32.372
Now, please continue this fantastic story about princesses.

07:32.372 --> 07:33.202
Yes.

07:33.702 --> 07:35.582
Nice pitch, Tama-chan.

07:37.712 --> 07:40.082
Now there are four of them.

07:40.672 --> 07:43.422
But there is only one umeboshi left.

07:43.422 --> 07:45.462
What shall we do?

07:45.462 --> 07:46.422
Oh, yes!

07:47.512 --> 07:50.802
The magic curtain!

07:50.802 --> 07:53.642
Now, let's multiply the umeboshi!

07:53.642 --> 07:55.642
chi-chin pui pui!

07:56.102 --> 07:57.142
Go!

07:57.682 --> 07:58.732
It was successful!

07:58.732 --> 08:00.602
Now there is another pot of umeboshi!

08:00.852 --> 08:03.482
Yay! It was successful!

08:03.482 --> 08:04.942
Oh?

08:04.942 --> 08:09.282
The magic curtain gave them an extra princess along with the extra pot of umeboshi.

08:09.782 --> 08:13.242
Now, with their umeboshi in hand, the five princesses are going...

08:13.242 --> 08:16.622
...mmmmm, it's so sour!

08:17.752 --> 08:22.332
I'm glad she has many friends... maybe.

08:22.332 --> 08:23.712
That's right.

08:23.712 --> 08:28.592
And it's a wonderful story... maybe.

08:29.132 --> 08:30.302
Thank you.

08:30.302 --> 08:31.092
I'm glad to hear that.

08:35.852 --> 08:38.602
He knows how to get to her heart!

08:41.602 --> 08:43.102
Momo-san, give me more!

08:44.442 --> 08:45.772
Sure!

08:45.772 --> 08:48.032
Here you go.

08:52.572 --> 08:53.662
Aaah!

08:59.832 --> 09:02.792
What will make Kozue-chan happy...

09:02.792 --> 09:05.172
That's so like him.

09:06.042 --> 09:09.512
He clearly modeled the story after Kozue-chan.

09:09.512 --> 09:14.552
I should ask <i>him</i> to model a film after me.

09:14.552 --> 09:18.972
Anything modeled after you would turn into a comedy horror.

09:18.972 --> 09:20.522
What?

09:28.482 --> 09:34.072
I want Kozue-chan to hear Shiratori-san's story too.

09:34.072 --> 09:34.992
Tama-chan...

09:36.372 --> 09:39.622
So, what should we cook?

09:39.622 --> 09:43.122
We have to have a big party for Kozue-chan's birthday!

09:43.122 --> 09:44.542
Right!

09:44.872 --> 09:47.712
What happens next?

09:47.712 --> 09:50.552
I want to know... maybe.

09:50.882 --> 09:53.922
Well, about that...

09:53.932 --> 09:55.512
I'm not done yet.

09:55.512 --> 09:56.222
Sorry.

10:05.732 --> 10:07.732
It looks lonely, maybe.

10:08.522 --> 10:12.692
It looks lonely around the castle... maybe.

10:13.242 --> 10:19.702
Princess Umeboshi should have many more friends... maybe.

10:20.832 --> 10:22.042
That's right!

10:23.042 --> 10:24.372
All right!

10:24.372 --> 10:26.792
Friends, friends...

10:29.632 --> 10:31.962
They haven't changed a bit.

10:57.532 --> 10:59.452
All right, done!

10:59.452 --> 11:00.452
How's this?

11:01.162 --> 11:06.462
Around Princess Umeboshi's castle, there lived some fun and funny friends.

11:06.462 --> 11:09.252
So it is lively around the castle once again.

11:09.252 --> 11:12.002
Sing for us, Princess!

11:12.002 --> 11:13.462
OK!

11:22.432 --> 11:24.432
What wonderful singing!

11:24.432 --> 11:26.392
Who is singing that?

11:26.392 --> 11:27.772
It's Princess Umeboshi.

11:27.772 --> 11:29.062
Princess Umeboshi?

11:29.062 --> 11:29.852
Oh?

11:32.362 --> 11:33.362
Nice to meet you.

11:33.732 --> 11:35.362
Nice to meet you.

11:38.112 --> 11:40.322
Nice to meet you, your Highness.

11:42.702 --> 11:44.912
Nice to meet you, your Grace.

11:45.242 --> 11:48.622
And that's how the prince and the princess met.

11:48.622 --> 11:49.292
But...

12:09.312 --> 12:12.232
The prince and company were swept away.

12:16.402 --> 12:19.702
Princess Umeboshi fell unconscious from the shock.

12:21.242 --> 12:23.622
What happens to Princess Umeboshi?

12:23.622 --> 12:24.532
And the prince?

12:25.452 --> 12:26.952
Don't give me that!

12:26.952 --> 12:27.792
Read the rest!

12:27.792 --> 12:29.872
What happens!?

12:29.872 --> 12:30.542
Yeah...

12:30.922 --> 12:32.002
Ahh!

12:32.002 --> 12:34.752
The prince got washed away along with the animals.

12:34.752 --> 12:36.042
Right then, the prince thought...

12:36.052 --> 12:37.672
..."Yes, that's it!"

12:37.672 --> 12:39.552
He took out his sketchbook and his crayon.

12:41.592 --> 12:43.432
All right, it's done!

12:46.242 --> 12:48.392
Thank you, Sharky Tamami-gon!

12:49.852 --> 12:51.272
Good!

12:51.272 --> 12:51.892
So...

12:51.892 --> 12:53.402
What's next!?

12:54.562 --> 12:56.272
Princess!

12:59.942 --> 13:01.862
Princess!

13:02.492 --> 13:03.952
Yes!

13:03.952 --> 13:05.912
Yay!

13:08.162 --> 13:12.412
So they were able to see each other again,

13:12.422 --> 13:15.752
except for the one Princess Umeboshi, who remained asleep.

13:18.552 --> 13:23.722
I'm glad they could meet the prince again... maybe.

13:24.052 --> 13:27.302
Anyway, their attire is correct.

13:27.312 --> 13:32.022
A charming prince and his friends make the best situation!

13:32.022 --> 13:33.942
But how could she be sleeping!

13:33.942 --> 13:35.102
That's irritating!

13:35.522 --> 13:37.112
That's right.

13:38.862 --> 13:41.782
<i>Now, what next?</i>

13:41.782 --> 13:43.112
<i>What should happen?</i>

13:55.422 --> 13:59.092
When the cricket pulled out the stopper,

13:59.842 --> 14:01.962
the water quickly drained.

14:02.762 --> 14:04.132
Yay!

14:04.132 --> 14:05.972
Princess Umeboshi!

14:06.682 --> 14:08.352
Yes!

14:09.222 --> 14:10.102
Oh?

14:10.102 --> 14:11.062
Look!

14:11.062 --> 14:14.022
There are no gates in the walls of Princess Umeboshi's castle.

14:14.022 --> 14:16.102
You can't enter or leave.

14:16.352 --> 14:17.102
What!?

14:17.102 --> 14:18.312
Why?

14:18.772 --> 14:20.112
Ouch!

14:21.282 --> 14:21.982
...maybe.

14:22.402 --> 14:24.282
Ta-daa!

14:24.282 --> 14:27.242
The magic sketchbook and crayons!

14:27.242 --> 14:29.622
The prince started to draw something.

14:36.002 --> 14:38.712
A rainbow bridge was drawn between there and Princess Umeboshi's castle.

14:38.712 --> 14:40.542
Yay!

14:40.542 --> 14:41.802
Thank you!

14:41.802 --> 14:44.262
Now we can get out of the castle.

14:44.672 --> 14:48.222
Now, come down the rainbow, Princess.

14:48.222 --> 14:49.222
Yes.

14:49.472 --> 14:50.182
Yes.

14:50.392 --> 14:51.052
Yes.

14:51.472 --> 14:52.062
Yes.

14:54.602 --> 14:55.892
It's a success!
Yay!

14:55.892 --> 14:56.002
It's a success!

14:56.002 --> 14:56.162
Yay!
It's a success!

14:56.162 --> 14:56.192
Yay!

14:56.192 --> 14:57.332
Princess Umeboshi was able to get out of the castle.
Yay!

14:57.332 --> 14:57.422
Princess Umeboshi was able to get out of the castle.

14:57.422 --> 14:58.882
Yay!
Princess Umeboshi was able to get out of the castle.

14:58.882 --> 14:58.982
Princess Umeboshi was able to get out of the castle.

14:58.982 --> 14:59.562
Yay!
Princess Umeboshi was able to get out of the castle.

14:59.562 --> 15:00.042
Yay!

15:00.612 --> 15:01.482
But...

15:01.482 --> 15:02.072
Oh?

15:02.362 --> 15:02.902
One...

15:03.322 --> 15:03.652
Two...

15:03.992 --> 15:04.402
Three...

15:04.742 --> 15:05.822
Four...

15:06.202 --> 15:08.112
There is one princess missing.

15:08.952 --> 15:13.082
There is one Princess Umeboshi who is still asleep inside the castle.

15:13.452 --> 15:16.122
So, the prince climbed up the rainbow.

15:16.122 --> 15:20.502
Go, Prince!

15:21.212 --> 15:22.172
Go! Go!

15:23.632 --> 15:25.012
Prince!

15:26.302 --> 15:28.132
Let's go!

15:29.182 --> 15:30.892
Go... maybe.

15:39.192 --> 15:41.192
Then what happens?

15:44.402 --> 15:48.652
S-so, the prince continues to walk across the rainbow.

15:49.032 --> 15:53.662
The friends are also very worried about the sleeping Princess Umeboshi.

15:54.292 --> 15:56.452
The other four Princess Umeboshi are worried too.

15:57.252 --> 15:58.712
Go, Prince!

15:59.832 --> 16:04.172
And so, the prince came upon the sleeping princess.

16:04.802 --> 16:05.882
And...

16:06.342 --> 16:08.552
"Wake up, Princess Umeboshi."

16:08.552 --> 16:10.092
"Everyone is worried about you."

16:11.842 --> 16:13.182
"Of course, I am too."

16:14.972 --> 16:18.102
And on the princess' cheek, the prince...

16:19.312 --> 16:23.192
Did the prince and everyone else's wish reach the princess' heart?

16:24.732 --> 16:26.362
Finally, Princess Umeboshi...

16:28.362 --> 16:29.862
...woke up.

16:36.542 --> 16:39.202
After being showered in a glaring light,

16:39.212 --> 16:40.962
the princesses turned into a brave warrior,

16:42.672 --> 16:44.922
a curious fairy,

16:46.502 --> 16:48.092
a fashionable dancer,

16:49.512 --> 16:51.092
and a skillful sorcerer.

17:03.062 --> 17:07.692
And that's how the prince was able to bring the princess back from her deep sleep.

17:09.692 --> 17:11.492
Everyone was so happy and...

17:16.702 --> 17:17.992
It's no good.

17:17.992 --> 17:19.202
No...

17:19.202 --> 17:21.582
It was good...

17:21.582 --> 17:24.002
But even Shiratori-kun can't do it?

17:25.042 --> 17:27.342
That's fun!

17:28.342 --> 17:30.842
So, what happens next?

17:31.052 --> 17:31.972
Hurry!

17:31.972 --> 17:33.842
Read more, Shiratori Onii-chan!

17:34.552 --> 17:35.842
More?

17:35.842 --> 17:37.762
Oh, how could you?

17:37.762 --> 17:40.352
He rescued the princess and he says good-bye?

17:40.602 --> 17:43.432
Princess Umeboshi is alone again...

17:43.442 --> 17:45.352
She's lonely... maybe.

17:46.482 --> 17:47.652
<i>How many more...</i>

17:48.942 --> 17:53.862
<i>How many more times will we be able to spend the seasons together?</i>

17:54.242 --> 17:58.242
<i>Everyone will eventually leave Narutakisou, right?</i>

18:00.872 --> 18:01.872
<i>I see.</i>

18:03.622 --> 18:05.372
<i>That's why Kozue-chan did...</i>

18:08.752 --> 18:10.672
The story isn't done yet.

18:11.842 --> 18:14.672
It has a happy ending, so sit back and listen.

18:18.642 --> 18:24.022
The prince takes sword mastery lessons from the warrior princess.

18:26.152 --> 18:29.942
He plays tag with the fairy princess.

18:32.652 --> 18:36.202
He learns how to dance from the dancing princess,

18:36.202 --> 18:37.492
and this comes next... eh!?

18:38.372 --> 18:42.742
And he was shown magic tricks by the magical princess.

18:44.832 --> 18:46.042
And...

18:46.042 --> 18:48.752
...Princess Umeboshi brought lots of umeboshi,

18:49.082 --> 18:51.252
and now it's time to eat umeboshi all at once.

18:52.672 --> 18:54.262
It's so sour!

18:54.762 --> 18:58.182
Spring, summer, fall, and winter.

18:58.892 --> 19:06.772
The prince, princess, and their friends in the forest lived together happily ever after.

19:07.982 --> 19:11.562
That was a wonderful story, Shiratori-san.

19:11.572 --> 19:12.862
Kozue-chan?

19:12.862 --> 19:14.112
Yes.

19:14.112 --> 19:15.492
Yay!

19:15.492 --> 19:16.112
Kozue-...

19:16.742 --> 19:18.822
I will never let go of you!

19:18.822 --> 19:19.862
Tamami-chan!

19:21.952 --> 19:23.832
Yeah!

19:23.832 --> 19:24.872
You've done it, Shiratori!

19:55.982 --> 19:57.652
Um, Sir...

19:58.032 --> 19:59.282
Sir...

19:59.282 --> 20:00.702
Shut up!

20:00.702 --> 20:01.532
Now what!?

20:01.532 --> 20:02.662
Madam is...

20:02.952 --> 20:04.662
Oh, Ushimitsu-san.

20:04.662 --> 20:09.662
I thought you had a meeting with the artist's committee?

20:09.672 --> 20:11.332
I-it got canceled.

20:11.332 --> 20:15.462
Then we have Kozue-chan's birthday party today.

20:15.462 --> 20:18.422
Would you come too, Grandpa Ushimitsu?

20:18.422 --> 20:19.842
What party!?

20:20.592 --> 20:21.682
Grandpa?

20:21.682 --> 20:26.182
You are Mom's dad, so you are my grandpa.

20:27.352 --> 20:29.182
Grandpa...

20:30.232 --> 20:31.392
Grandpa.

20:31.402 --> 20:32.902
Not you!

20:33.152 --> 20:36.442
That means Mahiru-sama is an aunty, right?

20:36.442 --> 20:37.402
Tachibana.

20:37.402 --> 20:38.152
Yes.

20:48.502 --> 20:51.122
It's such a fun birthday party.

20:52.082 --> 20:53.962
There are so many cute kids!

20:53.962 --> 20:55.292
Isn't Reiko-san around?

20:55.292 --> 20:57.382
My lovely Reiko-san!

20:57.422 --> 20:59.882
Reiko-san!
Would you not embarrass us?

20:59.882 --> 21:00.842
So, this is a commoners' party?
Would you not embarrass us?

21:00.842 --> 21:01.762
So, this is a commoners' party?

21:01.802 --> 21:04.182
It's not a good match for my tastes.

21:04.722 --> 21:06.262
Then I'll eat it for you.

21:07.562 --> 21:10.432
It's the inactive member's birthday party.

21:10.432 --> 21:12.392
So wonderful.

21:17.522 --> 21:19.692
That's a good picture.

21:19.692 --> 21:22.902
Yes, it's a good place, Grandma Yu.

21:23.362 --> 21:25.412
Who is the grandma?

21:27.492 --> 21:29.792
You've grown up to be so great, Kozue-chan!

21:29.792 --> 21:31.702
Yes, yes, I know.

21:31.712 --> 21:32.412
Yo, yo!

21:32.412 --> 21:34.462
Anyone want to try speculative trading?

21:34.462 --> 21:36.462
You can dream of getting rich by it!

21:36.962 --> 21:38.462
Onee-sama!

21:39.672 --> 21:41.842
You came!?

21:41.842 --> 21:42.672
Yes!

21:42.672 --> 21:45.052
We heard you were going overseas!

21:45.052 --> 21:47.932
Please don't go, Onee-sama!

21:47.932 --> 21:49.562
Oh, that?

21:49.562 --> 21:50.932
I'm not going.

21:51.392 --> 21:53.102
I told him firmly.

21:53.102 --> 21:55.602
"Come back and propose to me after your dream comes true."

21:55.602 --> 21:57.522
"And I'll wait until then."

21:58.232 --> 22:01.322
Onee-sama, you're great!

22:01.322 --> 22:03.862
Great job, Captain Momo.

22:04.912 --> 22:09.582
By the way, what happened to your whatever-it-was-called award, Haibara-san?

22:09.582 --> 22:12.792
Well, that company failed on a few things here and there,

22:12.792 --> 22:13.952
and went bankrupt.

22:13.962 --> 22:16.672
He's such a useless man, even luck wouldn't help him.

22:17.212 --> 22:18.922
I see.

22:18.922 --> 22:20.092
Hey, Tama.

22:20.092 --> 22:21.052
Yes.

22:21.052 --> 22:22.462
About this cake...

22:23.012 --> 22:26.472
Are there other girls who have their birthday today besides Kozue-chan?

22:26.972 --> 22:28.142
Yes.

22:28.142 --> 22:31.012
It's a birthday for a wonderful five.

22:31.892 --> 22:32.972
Kozue-chan.

22:33.522 --> 22:33.972
Yes.

22:34.392 --> 22:35.602
Just as I thought.

22:35.602 --> 22:37.602
You are the guest of honor today,

22:37.602 --> 22:39.312
so I'll handle things in here.

22:39.312 --> 22:42.532
But I wanted to eat this with everyone.

22:42.902 --> 22:43.362
Umeboshi!

22:43.942 --> 22:45.072
Yes!

22:45.072 --> 22:46.532
It will be delicious!

22:56.292 --> 23:00.962
Narutakisou is a precious place with lots of heartful memories.

23:00.962 --> 23:03.172
Let's keep on making lots of memories.

23:03.172 --> 23:03.672
Yes!

23:03.842 --> 23:05.692
Yeah, of course!

23:05.697 --> 23:08.302
Let's make lots and lots!

23:08.302 --> 23:09.392
Let's do it correctly!

23:09.392 --> 23:10.552
Correctly!

23:10.552 --> 23:12.182
It'll be fun... maybe.

23:13.722 --> 23:15.312
OK, all together...

23:15.312 --> 23:15.982
Yes.

23:18.942 --> 23:21.692
It's so sour!

23:29.492 --> 23:36.002
One day, I drew a picture all over a canvas,
itsu no hika canvas ni e ippai

23:36.082 --> 23:41.802
a picture of 7-colored dreams.
nanairo no yume egaita

23:43.222 --> 23:49.682
When I noticed, I was a bit more grown up.
ki ga tsukeba sukoshi otona ni natte

23:49.932 --> 23:54.982
What have I found?
nani wo mitsuketandarou

23:56.942 --> 24:03.692
In this aimless daily life,
yuka ate no nai mainichi no nakade

24:03.942 --> 24:09.622
I found something that's most important.
ichiban taisetsuna koto ni kizuita

24:10.622 --> 24:16.462
Yes, it's always all right,
donna tokidemo sousa daijoubu

24:16.462 --> 24:18.712
because you are here.
kimi ga irukara

24:18.922 --> 24:25.092
Holding these unforgettable thoughts,
wasurenai kono omoi dakishimete

24:25.592 --> 24:31.432
I will start walking the path of the halted fantasy again,
mouichido togireta yume no fantasy

24:31.432 --> 24:36.062
at my own speed.
aruitemiyou boku no speed de
